 089C   07F6    
 089C   07F6    '----- startup
 089C   07F6    tmo = 2
 089C   07F6    'COM() statements in this programme
 089C   07F6    '----- reset the 8253 timer (channel 0) to the standard 18.2 Hz
                 tick.  Win98
 089C   07F6    '      "MS-DOS mode" can hand off with channel 0 left reprogram
                med faster,
 089C   07F6    '      which shortens SOUND durations (the intro races past) an
                d skews TIMER
 089C   07F6    '      (the in-room clock) -- prime suspect for the MS-DOS-mode
                 rush + lock-up.
 089C   07F6    '      No-op on a healthy DOS boot (it's already 18.2 Hz there)
                .
 089C   07F6    OUT &H43, &H36
 089C   07F6    OUT &H40, 0
 089C   07F6    OUT &H40, 0
 089C   07F6    CALL InitVars
 08BB   07F6    CALL LoadConfig
 08C0   07F6    CALL initAllFonts(fontData(), font3Data(), fontbData())
 08D1   07F6    '----- guard Intro's cutscene sound loops on fast CPUs: QB's SO
                UND runtime
 08D1   07F6    '      can raise "Illegal function call" in the tight loops on 
                hardware far
 08D1   07F6    '      faster than this 1993 intro targets.  Intro has no handl
                er of its own
 08D1   07F6    '      (it runs before the ON ERROR GOTO errhand below).  RESUM
                E NEXT would
 08D1   07F6    '      need /X, which overflows the 64K module, so on such an e
                                                                      PAGE   5
                                                                      30 Jun 26
                                                                      18:25:51
Offset  Data    Source Line      Microsoft (R) QuickBASIC Compiler Version 4.50

                rror introSkip
 08D1   07F6    '      bails out of the cutscene to introDone -- the intro ends
                 early but the
 08D1   07F6    '      game runs instead of crashing to DOS.  (Throttle work re
                stores it.)
 08D1   07F6    ON ERROR GOTO introSkip
 08DB   07F6    IF inon <> 0 THEN CALL Intro
 08F6   07F6    introDone:
